<title>USA: Morrison Knudsen wins $30 mln Egypt contract.</title>
<headline>Morrison Knudsen wins $30 mln Egypt contract.</headline>
<dateline>BOISE, Idaho 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morrison Knudsen Corp said on Wednesday it was awarded a contract worth up to $30 million to rehabilitate and construct facilities at 19 military installations in Egypt.</p>
<p>The work for the Egyptian Air Force will be administered by the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers under a program called Pacer Forge Facility Support.</p>
<p>The contract, to be carried out on a cost-plus-fee basis, will cover an initial period of one year with four one-year options.</p>
